  "body": "I'm having a hard time figuring out what the internal slots of the various canvas objects are.\r\n\r\nA `canvas` element has a bitmap. A `CanvasRenderingContext2D` object has an **output bitmap**. If the `canvas` element's rendering context is a `CanvasRenderingContext2D` object, is its bitmap that objects's **output bitmap**?\r\n\r\nIf that is the case, why does a `CanvasRenderingContext2D` object need its own reference? Can it not go through the `canvas` element pointer? (Or vice versa, can the `canvas` element not go through the rendering context (which is also an implicit concept I think we should make explicit)?)\r\n\r\nI'd love if it we made this much more clear.\r\n\r\ncc @junov ",
